Subject: a region scroll leaves an overlay's own cells in place, not its whole row

0008 kept an overlay a program repaints inside its scrolling region (Claude Code's "Jump to
bottom" hint on its transcript's last row) from being drawn two or three times by drawing the
overlay's whole edge row in place and sliding only the rows between. But that row holds text too:
it showed its final line at once while the rows around it slid, so the same line was on screen
twice, one copy squeezed under the pinned row, and the row read as stuck.

The region now animates whole, edge rows included, and the overlay's own cells (the run
`repaintedInPlace` finds, no longer its row) are a hole in it: drawn where they are while the
content slides past and under them. The shaders take two holes per region (`region_hole`, one
for each edge row); a cell in a hole belongs to no region, content that would be drawn in one is
cut off there, and the hole's own cells are never drawn as part of the content. The hit test
leaves the cells unshifted too (`RegionHole`), so a click on the hint lands on it while the text
beside it still slides.

The rows that scroll out of the region become ghosts, and an edge row's ghost is made without the
overlay's columns (`ghostCells`). The hole only hides a ghost while it is in the hole's place: the
renderer often takes several of Claude Code's scrolls in one frame (they come about 5 ms apart
under a trackpad flick), and each makes its ghosts from the frame before, so the second scroll's
copy of the old bottom row, hint included, started a row above the hole and slid down the region
as a second hint.

The overlay also covers text. Scrolled back, the new bottom row is a line that was a few rows higher
in the frame before; the program draws the hint over its middle, so the terminal holds nothing
there, and the line slid into the hint's row with a hint-shaped blank in it. The text comes from
the row it slid from: a ghost row of just the overlay's columns (`overlayFills`, `columnCells`),
drawn with the content, fills the blank until the hint covers it (the shaders look for it where a
hole's cells would be drawn as content).

Calm's own patch (not from thdxg/ghostty); applies on top of 0011, replacing the pinned rows
(`PinnedEdges`) 0008 added with holes.

